Add a thumbnail image to the top right, I think for each Wikipedia article there's like one canonical main image. So we want a fairly low resolution version of that. Include any caption that comes with it underneath like a normal caption. Then have that thumbnail image also be what displays in the media player.

## Implementation (2026-10-24)

- `WikipediaRepository` now extracts the canonical main image before DOM scrubbing
  (infobox image first, then leading figure/thumb) via `.infobox img, figure img,
  .thumb img, .mw-file-description img`. The low-res rendered `<img src>` is
  resolved to an absolute https URL, and the caption comes from
  `.infobox-caption` / `figcaption` / `.thumbcaption`. Returns
  `FetchedArticle(sections, image)`.
- `ArticleImage(url, caption)` model added; `UiState.Article` carries `image`.
- New `ThumbnailCache` downloads the thumb (~tens of KB) to
  `filesDir/thumbnails/<titleHash>.img`; the ViewModel exposes `thumbFile`.
- `ArticleScreen` shows the image right-aligned under the title with its caption
  beneath (decoded off the main thread, appears once downloaded).
- Media player artwork: `TtsPlayer` sets `MediaMetadata.artworkUri`, fed through
  `WcastMediaService.startService/onPlaybackStarted` with a local file URI (or
  remote URL fallback).
- Bookmark codec/store persist the image (url + caption) so offline articles keep
  their thumbnail reference; round-trip covered by a new unit test.
- Verified: `assembleDebug` + `testDebugUnitTest` pass; APK regenerated. 